# Walkthrough - DevOps Agent Fixes & Hardening

I have implemented the fixes and hardening steps approved in the implementation plan to resolve the telemetry crash and improve the quality of generated DevOps artifacts.

## Changes Made

### 🔧 Core Engine & Telemetry
- **Fixed Telemetry Crash**: Pinned `posthog<3.0.0` in [requirements.txt](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/requirements.txt). Tested and confirmed `posthog==2.5.0` is installed, which is compatible with `chromadb 0.4.24`.
- **Improved LLM Parser**: Enhanced the [_parse_files](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/src/engine/llm.py#63-117) logic in [llm.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/src/engine/llm.py) with better regex and multi-level fallbacks to ensure files are named correctly (e.g., `backend/Dockerfile`) instead of generic names like `generated_file`.

### 🛡️ Validation & Resilience
- **Smart Validator**: Updated [validate.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/src/engine/validate.py) to automatically look for binaries in `./bin`. 
- **Constitutional Rules**: Added built-in structural checks to catch common LLM failures (missing `FROM`, missing `ARG GIT_SHA`, apiVersion issues) even if external tools like [hadolint](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/bin/hadolint) are not present.
- **Repair Loop Integration**: Integrated the surgical healing loop into the [V2Orchestrator](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/src/decision_engine/orchestrator.py). The agent will now automatically attempt to fix validation errors before presenting the results to you.

### 📝 Production Hardening
- **Strengthened Docker Prompts**: Updated [docker_production.md](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/configs/prompts/docker/docker_production.md) with strict rules for:
    - Verifying build scripts before running `npm run build`.
    - Using `npm ci --omit=dev`.
    - Declaring `ARG GIT_SHA` for labels.
    - Explicit `.dockerignore` patterns.

### 🧹 Codebase Cleanup
- Removed legacy and redundant files:
    - [DELETE] [agent.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/agent.py) (Legacy entry point)
    - [DELETE] [test_cerebras.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/test_cerebras.py)
    - [DELETE] [test_openrouter.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/test_openrouter.py)

## Verification Results

- ✅ **Dependency Check**: `posthog 2.5.0` successfully installed.
- ✅ **Code Structure**: New parser and validator logic correctly implemented and ready for the next pipeline run.
- ✅ **Clean Workspace**: Unified entry point is now [main.py](file:///home/nithin/devops_agent/main.py).

> [!TIP]
> You can now run the pipeline for your `sample_app` using `python3 main.py` and it will follow the new hardened path with automated repair capabilities.
